---
// layout
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import { getGeneratedOgImage } from "@utils/og-image";

const lastUpdated = "Sep 2026";
const ogImage = getGeneratedOgImage("pages", "now");
---

<PageLayout
  tabTitle="Now"
  description="What I'm focused on at this point in my life."
  image={ogImage}
>
  <section>
    <h1>/now</h1>
    <p class="hero-text">
      A list of things I'm focused on at this point in my life.
    </p>
    <p class="updated-date">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Orbit is in its refinement phase:</strong> I'm not actively adding
        new features right now. I'm making the existing product more robust,
        working through edge cases, improving onboarding, and making the flows
        easier to understand. I'm also tightening the design language so the whole
        app feels more consistent. Orbit isn't growing much at the moment, so I'm
        also figuring out how to distribute it and reach real users beyond the
        people I already talk to, without paying for ads.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Learning about Android development:</strong> I'm mostly trying to
        understand the landscape before choosing a direction. I'm looking at the
        different ways to build and publish an Android application, and the
        trade-offs between them. I'm not focused on learning Kotlin, Dart, or
        React Native in isolation yet. Those are tools I can pick up when I have
        something to build. Right now, I want to understand the architectural
        choices first, then learn the required tools while building.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Writing more:</strong> I've started capturing thoughts, questions,
        lessons, and opinions as they come up, then returning to them later and
        turning some of them into notes. I don't publish everything, but writing has
        become a useful way to process what I'm learning.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Looking for the right opportunity:</strong> I'm not actively
        searching for a job, but I am open to working on an excellent product with
        people who care about what they're building. Getting paid is obviously part
        of that, but what I'm really looking for is the kind of work that's enjoyable
        to show up for.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Movies are still my escape hatch:</strong> watching plenty of them,
        as usual, whenever I need to switch off.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <blockquote>
      <h3>Wait, what is this?</h3>
      <p>
        It's a concept popularized by{" "}
        <a href="https://sive.rs/nowff" target="_blank">
          Derek Sivers<Icon
            name="lucide:arrow-up-right"
            size={14}
            class="ext-arrow"
          />
        </a>. A /now page shares what you'd tell a friend you hadn't seen for a
        while.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <style>
    .updated-date {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
      font-style: italic;
    }
  </style>
</PageLayout>
